#include <rooms.h>

inherit "/std/room";



void create() {

  ::create();

  set_property("light", 2);

  set_property("indoors", 1);

  set_property("no attack", 1);

  set_property("no scry", 1);

  set_property("no teleport", 1);

  set_property("no summon", 1);

  set_property("no cast", 1);

  set("long", "This is the waiting room, you are in the creation process.");

}

// /d/standard/setter.lpc's pick() moves a player here BEFORE the
// multi-step do_rolls()/input_to() stat-assignment sequence has finished
// setting "dev points" -- and this room has zero exits and no add_action
// commands of its own (the "pick"/"read" actions live on the setter room,
// which the player already left). A player who disconnects (link death,
// or just closing the client) anywhere in that sequence -- rather than
// reaching the final "yes" confirmation -- loses the pending input_to()
// callback across the reconnect (the driver does not carry a pending
// input_to across an exec()'d reconnect), and comes back into a
// dead-end room with no way to resume creation and no way to leave it:
// permanently soft-locked, with only wizard intervention (trans/goto) as
// a way out. Also reachable via daemon/reinc_d.lpc's reincarnation path,
// which moves players back through the same ROOM_SETTER flow. Restart
// the stat-assignment step from scratch (no partial progress was ever
// saved to the player object -- pick() resets "__creation_complete" to 0
// and setter.lpc's yes_or_no() is the only place that ever sets it back
// to 1, right when "in creation" itself goes back to 0) whenever a
// living reconnects/re-enters here with character creation still
// incomplete.
//
// Deliberately NOT keyed on "dev points" being unset: a REINCARNATING
// character (daemon/reinc_d.lpc moves them back through this same
// ROOM_SETTER flow to re-pick a race) already has a real, nonzero "dev
// points" left over from their previous life, so that property alone
// can't distinguish "never finished this pick()" from "finished a
// previous life's pick()" -- see setter.lpc's pick() for the same note.
//
// IMPORTANT: pick()'s own move() into this room synchronously triggers
// THIS init() too (move_object()'s setup_new_commands(), same as any
// room entry) -- before pick() gets to call do_rolls() itself on the very
// next line. Without the "__setup_in_progress" guard below, that first,
// completely normal entry would also match the "still incomplete"
// condition and call do_rolls() a SECOND, reentrant time while the first
// call is still unwinding, corrupting the driver's action/sentence list
// (live-reproduced: a driver segfault in add_action.cc's user_parser ->
// mudlib_stats add_moves(), dereferencing a stale sentence->ob, on the
// very next command after a brand-new character's first-ever "pick
// <race>" -- see NOTES.md for the full writeup). pick() sets
// "__setup_in_progress" immediately before its own move()+do_rolls() and
// clears it immediately after, so this guard is only ever false during
// pick()'s own single, correct call -- true on every genuine
// reconnect-into-an-unfinished-creation, since that always happens well
// after pick() has already returned.
void init() {
  ::init();
  if (living(this_player()) && this_player()->query("in creation") &&
    !this_player()->query("__creation_complete") &&
    !this_player()->query("__setup_in_progress")) {
    write("\nYour character creation was interrupted -- restarting stat "
      "assignment.\n");
    ROOM_SETTER->do_rolls();
  }
}
